00:25:57.430 --> 00:25:59.730
signed william peele cdc etc etc

00:26:00.440 --> 00:26:03.660
And, uh, Annie, fax me a copy up here when you transcribe it, will you?

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:04.360
Thanks.

00:26:07.450 --> 00:26:12.570
Excuse me, what are you doing?

00:26:14.850 --> 00:26:15.510
Watching you.

00:26:16.100 --> 00:26:16.360
Why?

00:26:17.460 --> 00:26:21.720
I just want to see the guy who's stuck at Sheriff Buck.

00:26:23.410 --> 00:26:25.240
Did that make you uneasy?

00:26:26.330 --> 00:26:27.020
No.

00:26:27.600 --> 00:26:29.630
Um, nothing makes me uneasy.

00:26:31.050 --> 00:26:34.890
Except maybe seeing someone sitting on her ass in the middle of an emergency.

00:26:37.810 --> 00:26:45.110
Well, I'm flattered you even noticed my ass in the middle of this big emergency.

00:27:18.170 --> 00:27:18.980
- So you came.

00:27:18.980 --> 00:27:28.290
- Wait.

00:27:33.710 --> 00:27:35.310
But it's not about anything else.

00:27:38.620 --> 00:27:40.070
No heart, no soul.

00:27:41.480 --> 00:27:42.180
That's the way you want it?

00:27:42.620 --> 00:27:43.810
That's the way I want it.

00:30:46.700 --> 00:30:48.740
- She just started bleeding.

00:30:48.740 --> 00:30:51.500
- What were you doing at the time?

00:30:51.500 --> 00:30:56.100
- Never mind.

00:30:56.100 --> 00:30:57.940
- What's your relationship to Miss Emery?

00:31:00.280 --> 00:31:02.280
Buck, that's none of your business.

00:31:02.790 --> 00:31:03.750
We always gonna do this?

00:31:03.810 --> 00:31:04.170
Do what?

00:31:04.440 --> 00:31:05.480
Jerk around like this.

00:31:05.540 --> 00:31:07.120
You just make damn sure she gets better.

00:31:07.860 --> 00:31:09.080
Or you'll what?

00:31:09.140 --> 00:31:09.940
I'll think of something.

00:31:12.110 --> 00:31:14.030
Well, don't give yourself a brain hemorrhage.

00:31:16.190 --> 00:31:18.010
While you're at it, think about this.

00:31:19.640 --> 00:31:20.710
You need me, don't you?

00:31:21.950 --> 00:31:23.470
All right, I need you to fix her up.

00:31:23.530 --> 00:31:24.370
Just get on with it.

00:31:25.180 --> 00:31:25.840
I will.

00:31:29.260 --> 00:31:30.000
But then...

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.740
- Then what?

00:31:32.740 --> 00:31:51.460
- Then you'll owe me.

00:31:51.460 --> 00:31:53.280
- Hey.

00:31:53.280 --> 00:31:56.120
- I'm sorry, do I know you?

00:31:56.120 --> 00:31:57.830
- No, not yet.

00:31:57.830 --> 00:31:59.350
- I like that not yet part.

00:32:00.480 --> 00:32:03.040
- Selina Coons.

00:32:03.040 --> 00:32:07.450
You're the epidemiologist from Atlanta?

00:32:07.450 --> 00:32:09.700
- St. Charles, Louisiana, actually.

00:32:09.700 --> 00:32:11.460
It's got a one-room studio in Atlanta

00:32:11.460 --> 00:32:12.700
with one box of stuff in it

00:32:12.700 --> 00:32:15.760
I still hadn't unpacked since my last assignment.

00:32:15.760 --> 00:32:16.870
- What was that?

00:32:16.870 --> 00:32:21.140
- East Africa, cholera epidemic.

00:32:21.140 --> 00:32:24.850
- Well, this town must seem pretty tame after Africa.

00:32:24.850 --> 00:32:27.120
- Not so far.

00:32:27.120 --> 00:32:29.250
- Well, it's hard for outsiders here.

00:32:30.570 --> 00:32:32.070
Must feel like a fish out of water.

00:32:32.520 --> 00:32:35.240
Yeah, I feel kind of like the only normal guy in the nuthouse.

00:32:36.430 --> 00:32:38.210
You know, present company excluded, of course.

00:32:39.150 --> 00:32:41.390
Don't jump to conclusions.

00:32:45.270 --> 00:32:46.750
Anyway, I got a message for you.

00:32:47.540 --> 00:32:49.940
Oh, so this wasn't just a chance meeting.

00:32:50.830 --> 00:32:52.410
Oh, I'm taking a chance, all right.

00:32:54.190 --> 00:32:55.410
Look out for Sheriff Buck.

00:32:55.870 --> 00:32:56.850
Oh, come on.

00:32:56.890 --> 00:32:57.490
No, really.

00:32:59.430 --> 00:33:00.000
Have you ever looked...

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:02.200
Have you looked into the face of evil?

00:33:02.200 --> 00:33:07.710
I mean, the pure, unadulterated thing?

00:33:07.710 --> 00:33:10.660
I would probably be too busy to even notice it.

00:33:10.660 --> 00:33:16.640
You will.

00:33:56.360 --> 00:33:57.590
If you want to, you can go in.

00:34:00.670 --> 00:34:03.990
It's okay, uh, he's not contagious.

00:34:19.620 --> 00:34:24.920
I'm dwelling in the house, Caleb.

00:34:33.550 --> 00:34:38.510
It's going to be all right, Dr. Mann.

00:34:38.510 --> 00:34:39.960
Everything's going to be all right.

00:35:00.540 --> 00:35:02.370
- So what do you want?

00:35:02.370 --> 00:35:03.510
- You to link.

00:35:03.510 --> 00:35:05.840
I can feel it.

00:35:05.840 --> 00:35:09.290
- I thought scientists went on facts, not feelings.

00:35:09.290 --> 00:35:12.920
- Chasing viruses, it's a whole new field.

00:35:12.920 --> 00:35:16.280
We rely on our guts as well as data.

00:35:16.280 --> 00:35:18.280
Maybe you're an unwitting host.

00:35:18.280 --> 00:35:20.460
Maybe there's a symbiotic relationship

00:35:20.460 --> 00:35:23.380
between you and the infected that you're not aware of.

00:35:23.380 --> 00:35:25.020
- Maybe some monkeys run around Trinity

00:35:25.020 --> 00:35:26.720
doing his thing with bored housewives.

00:35:30.320 --> 00:35:33.360
How come every time you whisper in someone's ear, blood pours out?

00:35:34.730 --> 00:35:39.290
I mean, you give that fisheye of yours to some poor bastard, and he's down for the count.

00:35:40.890 --> 00:35:46.410
And how come, with all that kind of contact, you ain't sick?

00:35:48.570 --> 00:35:49.110
Right living.

00:35:49.990 --> 00:35:51.670
You've been in Africa too long, friend.

00:35:51.910 --> 00:35:53.070
You sound like a witch doctor.

00:35:53.410 --> 00:35:54.290
Roll up your sleeve.

00:35:54.780 --> 00:35:55.680
Oh, not this again.

00:35:55.680 --> 00:35:56.180
No, no.

00:35:56.400 --> 00:35:58.040
This time it's not a game.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:15.980
up your sleeve. I need a sample. I'll give you my blood. You'll be giving me yours. Peel. Kind of

00:36:15.980 --> 00:36:30.000
funny how these days thing we fear the most is our very lifeblood. Yeah, hysterical. So what do you do with this?

00:36:31.080 --> 00:36:35.770
- Yeah, we'll send it down to Atlanta, then we wait.

00:36:35.770 --> 00:36:36.930
- And you think it'll show what?

00:36:36.930 --> 00:36:38.430
That I'm the plague sower?

00:36:38.430 --> 00:36:44.810
Typhoid Mary?

00:36:44.810 --> 00:36:46.080
- I'll let you know.

00:36:46.080 --> 00:36:50.300
- Yeah.

00:36:50.300 --> 00:36:53.000
- All right, people, now the sheriff is not here

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:55.660
and I'm not authorized to make any statements about anything.

00:36:55.660 --> 00:36:58.290
- Come on, Ben, just give us the death toll.

00:36:58.290 --> 00:36:59.400
- It's so morbid.

00:36:59.400 --> 00:37:00.000
- What is it, five?

00:37:00.350 --> 00:37:02.890
Eight? Have they closed the elementary school yet?

00:37:02.890 --> 00:37:04.110
No, we haven't.

00:37:04.110 --> 00:37:07.830
Um, look, we don't want people to get all panicky just because--

00:37:07.830 --> 00:37:10.490
Just because the Trinity River has turned red?

00:37:10.490 --> 00:37:11.670
What is that about?

00:37:11.670 --> 00:37:15.990
Well, what that's about, friend, is an unfortunate red dye spill

00:37:15.990 --> 00:37:19.410
at a paper mill upriver in North Carolina, just south of Wilmington.

00:37:19.410 --> 00:37:22.360
Now, I've been in contact with the public authorities up there,

00:37:22.360 --> 00:37:25.230
and they've assured me that the malfunction has been corrected.

00:37:25.230 --> 00:37:27.230
All right? Anything else?

00:37:27.230 --> 00:37:30.000
Have you also been in contact with the investigator from the CDC

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:36.480
Yes, ma'am, I have. He's helping me with my investigation, and I have offered him my full cooperation as well.

00:37:38.820 --> 00:37:40.440
Ben, you want to bring your car around for me?

00:38:04.760 --> 00:38:19.450
- Now what?

00:38:19.450 --> 00:38:22.840
- Nothing out here on the night.

00:38:22.840 --> 00:38:26.020
- That's it for what, men?

00:38:26.020 --> 00:38:27.240
- Spirits?

00:38:53.960 --> 00:38:55.890
protect us all on a night like this.

00:39:23.260 --> 00:39:29.060
trying time for me. My people are afraid and I haven't been able to help them. So I thought

00:39:47.310 --> 00:40:00.000
thought what thought you could help me out I mean it's blood no offense Murley but that's kind of heavy

00:40:01.080 --> 00:40:04.530
I know it's your job to keep people on the straight and narrow.

00:40:04.950 --> 00:40:05.510
I've been there.

00:40:06.840 --> 00:40:08.220
And it's easy to get carried away.

00:40:08.860 --> 00:40:10.160
You lose sight of your goals.

00:40:10.700 --> 00:40:11.380
Protect the good.

00:40:12.880 --> 00:40:14.250
Punish the wicked.

00:40:15.160 --> 00:40:17.320
Or is the whole thing one big ego trip?

00:40:17.840 --> 00:40:19.280
You start to lose yourself.

00:40:21.450 --> 00:40:23.290
You start to fall.

00:40:23.430 --> 00:40:25.270
No, you are the one who has fallen, not me.

00:40:25.350 --> 00:40:26.090
You need me.

00:40:27.500 --> 00:40:28.300
I can show you.

00:40:30.350 --> 00:40:31.550
"I know what I'm doing."

00:40:31.550 --> 00:40:37.030
"Ah!"

00:40:37.030 --> 00:40:41.170
"Murnit! Murnit!"

00:40:41.170 --> 00:40:57.330
"Lord, buggy or nothing, but things are really getting out of hand."

00:40:57.330 --> 00:40:59.950
"And if you could make my cousin Gil all better..."

00:41:01.120 --> 00:41:29.760
poor old dr matt lord they didn't do nothing that's not exactly true caleb says who says me

00:41:30.060 --> 00:41:33.480
I saw Dr. Matt lying to the people, telling them that nothing had happened.

00:41:33.740 --> 00:41:35.800
He's just calming them down. That's his job.

00:41:36.220 --> 00:41:38.480
Well, they won't get crazy and turn on each other.

00:41:38.670 --> 00:41:40.010
Well, he should have told the truth.

00:41:40.390 --> 00:41:43.590
Lucas's job is to lie, to deceive.

00:41:44.680 --> 00:41:47.980
Well, he's got Matt now. He owns him.

00:41:48.060 --> 00:41:50.060
Cut it out, Murley. It's just an old guy.

00:41:53.100 --> 00:41:57.330
You're doing this, ain't you?

00:41:58.620 --> 00:42:00.000
You made him sick.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.000
And Gail?

00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:03.300
Gail made herself sick.

00:42:03.300 --> 00:42:04.300
She lay down with Lucas.

00:42:04.300 --> 00:42:05.300
Stop it, Murley.

00:42:05.300 --> 00:42:07.650
What's happened to you?

00:42:07.650 --> 00:42:12.230
Well, I was told to punish the wicked and warn those that would sin.

00:42:12.230 --> 00:42:13.230
Who told you this?

00:42:13.230 --> 00:42:16.170
You listen them voices too like Dr. Matt?

00:42:16.170 --> 00:42:17.180
Then maybe you're crazy.

00:42:17.180 --> 00:42:19.130
You just leave him alone.

00:42:19.130 --> 00:42:22.680
Leave us all alone.

00:42:22.680 --> 00:42:23.740
Well, but they've sinned, Caleb.

00:42:23.740 --> 00:42:25.740
Not like you have, Murley.

00:42:25.740 --> 00:42:26.740
Not by a long shot.

00:42:26.740 --> 00:42:30.000
And what about me?

00:42:30.280 --> 00:42:31.480
I spent time with Lucas.

00:42:31.910 --> 00:42:33.710
You gonna make me sick and crazy, too?

00:42:34.270 --> 00:42:35.140
Well, of course not.

00:42:35.160 --> 00:42:35.880
I love you.

00:42:36.160 --> 00:42:37.660
Well, then love them, too, Murley.

00:42:37.970 --> 00:42:38.760
All of them.

00:42:40.360 --> 00:42:42.160
All of us down here, we need it.

00:43:52.520 --> 00:43:56.180
-Leaving without saying goodbye, Billy?

00:43:56.180 --> 00:43:58.060
-Not leaving.

00:43:58.060 --> 00:43:59.000
-Sticking around.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:00.960
What for?

00:44:00.960 --> 00:44:04.520
To collect. You still owe me.

00:44:04.520 --> 00:44:06.800
Looks like the deal's been consummated already.

00:44:06.800 --> 00:44:11.170
Well, not our deal. We ain't even started yet.

00:44:11.170 --> 00:44:17.800
We haven't.

00:44:34.410 --> 00:44:36.210
How you feeling?

00:44:36.210 --> 00:44:37.440
I feel fine.

00:44:37.440 --> 00:44:42.150
You?

00:44:42.150 --> 00:44:42.870
I'm okay.
